(Bug #57's control. Refusing the absent value in a concretely-typed slot must
 not narrow the positions LANGUAGE.md:2659-2661 gives it - a list slot, a map
 value, and a `value` parameter or return - nor the defaults table's `Create a
 value called v.` (LANGUAGE.md:498), nor the three spellings of the literal.
 Every line below is a documented position, and every one of them compiled and
 ran correctly before the fix too: this test exists to prove the fix took
 nothing away.)

print nothing.
print null.
print nil.

a list called slots is [1, nothing, "x"].
print slots.
if element 2 of slots is nothing, print "the middle slot is absent".
if element 1 of slots is not nothing, print "the first slot is not".

a map called readings is {"found": 4, "absent": nothing}.
print readings.
if readings's "absent" is nothing, print "the key is present and absent".

a value called slot is nothing.
print slot.
if slot is nothing, print "a value holds it".

Create a value called unset.
print unset.

set slot to "now it holds text".
print slot.
set slot to nothing.
print slot.

To echo with a value called given. Return a value, given.

print echo of nothing.
if echo of nothing is nothing, print "through a value parameter and back".

Set element 1 of slots to nothing.
print slots.

Set readings's "found" to nothing.
print readings.

a text called greeting is "unharmed".
a list called counts is [1, 2].
a map called ages is {"bo": 42}.
print greeting.
print counts.
print ages.
